{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1480931-buying-merits-how-to-explain","id":1480931,"title":"Buying Merits how to explain?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-12T22:40:36-07:00","id":1480931,"title":"Buying Merits how to explain?","content":"how to explain buying merits other than resources or retainers or contact which need events in story to justify them<br /> <br /> <br /> some thinking and I think I have some ideas<br /> <br /> various fighting style merits require time in a dojo<br /> <br /> Meditative mind is acquired by meditating reading books or watching videos on meditation.<br /> <br /> know princess the hopeful is a fan game but I am strongly curious on how an otherwise mundane person would gain the dream travel merit.<br /> <br /> only means I Can see is to make the journey a time or two without it probably with a princess's help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T23:05:52-07:00","id":1480936,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that Merits have a degree of narrative abstraction. Having the Merit means you <i>have that game-mechanical effect available. </i>You can have allies without having Allies or status without having Status. Similarly, you can know martial arts without the Martial Arts Merit, or have an eye for the strange without Eye for the Strange.<br /> <br /> Which is to say one possible answer is that buying the Merit doesn't represent some diegetic change in the character's skillset or background, but could just be &quot;locking in&quot; the applicable benefits, like a plot beat in a movie where a character's skills become relevant to the focus of the action. Where did the character's Contacts or Marksmanship training come from? Well, if they have an appropriate background that makes sense, maybe they were already there. They just didn't come up.<br /> <br /> Talking with your Storyteller and conversing about where your characters are going can help. A supernatural Merit that's difficult to otherwise introduce could be set up in play by an encounter with some manner of anomaly or other ambiguously transformative experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T05:31:52-07:00","id":1480955,"title":"","content":"The easiest way to explain alot of merits is the character was doing required stuff in their downtime. The game often assumes resourses to come from a job for example and that day job/life happens off screen with actual play focusing on events important to the narrative. If you are worried about other characters being suprised by the new abilities you can easily play that off as the character having not told them that they were practicing such as they were embarassed or even just no point mentioning it before you can actually do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T11:15:25-07:00","id":1480980,"title":"","content":"I can also see some stuff justified by having just been out of practice or out of shape. You knew how to do Parkour but after fifteen years you're still a bit rusty.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Merits are more about getting the mechanical benefit. While most can almost certainly be trained for to a certain extent I think many STs would accept justifications along the lines of 'I always had a large number of occult times, I just never used them and so had to dig them out of storage'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 05-13-2022, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}